'

I'll now update the package.json to use Vue 2 and prepare the necessary files for our Trilogoweb portfolio. First, I'll modify the package.json to replace Vue 3 with Vue 2:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "package.json",
            "to_replace": "  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"vue\": \"^3.4.37\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-vue\": \"^5.1.2\",",
            "new_content": "  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"vue\": \"^2.6.14\",\n    \"vue-router\": \"^3.5.3\",\n    \"axios\": \"^0.27.2\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-vue2\": \"^2.3.1\","
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to update the vite.config.js to work with Vue 2 instead of Vue 3:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "vite.config.js",
            "to_replace": "import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport vue from '@vitejs/plugin-vue'\n\n// https://vitejs.dev/config/\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [vue()],\n})",
            "new_content": "import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport vue2 from '@vitejs/plugin-vue2'\n\n// https://vitejs.dev/config/\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [vue2()],\n})"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to create the necessary Vue component files for our portfolio website. First, let's create the directory structure for our views and components:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Terminal.run",
        "args": {
            "cmd": "mkdir -p src/views src/components src/assets/images"
        }
    }
]
```

Now let's update the App.vue file to create a layout with navigation for our portfolio website:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create the main App.vue file with navigation layout using Vue 2 syntax. This will serve as the main wrapper for all pages, containing the header with navigation menu and footer. The design emphasizes simplicity, speed, and clarity focused on results.",
            "paths": ["src/App.vue"]    
        }
    }
]
```

