metagpt.actions.add_requirement.UserRequ.content:
I'll create an impressive portfolio website called Trilogoweb using Vue 2. Let's start by navigating to the template directory and examining the existing structure.

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Terminal.run",
        "args": {
            "cmd": "cd vue_template && ls -la"
        }
    }
]
```

Let's start by checking the README.md file to understand the template better.

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "README.md"
        }
    }
]
```

I notice the template is using Vue 3, but the requirement is for Vue 2. Let me check the package.json and other key files to understand what we need to modify for our Vue 2-based portfolio website.

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "package.json"
        }
    }
]
```

I see that the template is using Vue 3, but we need to use Vue 2 for this project as requested. Let me check the main Vue file and then update the dependencies to use Vue 2 instead.

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "src/App.vue"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll check the main.js file to understand the Vue initialization setup:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "src/main.js"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll check the style.css file to understand the current styling approach:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "src/style.css"
        }
    }
]
```

I'll now update the package.json to use Vue 2 and prepare the necessary files for our Trilogoweb portfolio. First, I'll modify the package.json to replace Vue 3 with Vue 2:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "package.json",
            "to_replace": "  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"vue\": \"^3.4.37\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-vue\": \"^5.1.2\",",
            "new_content": "  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"vue\": \"^2.6.14\",\n    \"vue-router\": \"^3.5.3\",\n    \"axios\": \"^0.27.2\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-vue2\": \"^2.3.1\","
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to update the vite.config.js to work with Vue 2 instead of Vue 3:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "vite.config.js",
            "to_replace": "import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport vue from '@vitejs/plugin-vue'\n\n// https://vitejs.dev/config/\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [vue()],\n})",
            "new_content": "import { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport vue2 from '@vitejs/plugin-vue2'\n\n// https://vitejs.dev/config/\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [vue2()],\n})"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to create the necessary Vue component files for our portfolio website. First, let's create the directory structure for our views and components:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Terminal.run",
        "args": {
            "cmd": "mkdir -p src/views src/components src/assets/images"
        }
    }
]
```

Now let's update the App.vue file to create a layout with navigation for our portfolio website:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create the main App.vue file with navigation layout using Vue 2 syntax. This will serve as the main wrapper for all pages, containing the header with navigation menu and footer. The design emphasizes simplicity, speed, and clarity focused on results.",
            "paths": ["src/App.vue"]    
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll create the Home view component for our website, which will showcase the core value proposition of Trilogoweb:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create the Home page component that serves as the landing page for Trilogoweb. This page will focus on building trust with potential clients by highlighting how the website owner helps businesses grow through high-converting websites. It will include sections for a hero banner, key services, benefits, testimonials, and a strong call-to-action.",
            "paths": ["src/views/Home.vue"]
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll create the About page component for our website:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create the About page component that explains the mission and expertise of Trilogoweb. This page will focus on building trust and credibility by sharing the owner's story, expertise in creating high-converting websites, and the business philosophy behind Trilogoweb.",
            "paths": ["src/views/About.vue"]
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll create the Portfolio view component:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create the Portfolio page component that showcases past projects with clear, visual case studies demonstrating real business impact. This page will highlight the results achieved for previous clients, focusing on growth, increased sales, and better conversions.",
            "paths": ["src/views/Portfolio.vue"]
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll create the Contact page component:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create the Contact page component with a form for potential clients to get in touch, including options for different project types, budgets, and timelines to help prequalify leads. The form should be designed to capture essential information to understand client needs.",
            "paths": ["src/views/Contact.vue"]
        }
    }
]
```

I need to create the directory structure for the assets/images that will be needed by our portfolio website:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Terminal.run",
        "args": {
            "cmd": "mkdir -p public/assets/images"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to modify the main index.html file to update the title of our website:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "index.html",
            "to_replace": "  <title>Vite + Vue</title>",
            "new_content": "  <title>Trilogoweb - High-Converting Website Design & Development</title>"
        }
    }
]
```

I need to create placeholder images for our website to ensure it displays properly:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create SVG placeholder images for the website. These will serve as temporary visual elements until the client provides actual images. I'll create simple SVGs for hero image, mission illustration, expertise illustration, and telegram integration.",
            "paths": ["public/assets/images/hero-image.svg", "public/assets/images/mission.svg", "public/assets/images/expertise.svg", "public/assets/images/telegram-integration.svg"]
        }
    }
]
```

I'll create placeholder JavaScript files instead that will dynamically generate simple SVG-like images within our components:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create a utility JavaScript file that will help us create placeholder images for our website. This will allow us to generate simple colored rectangles or patterns as placeholders until the client provides actual images.",
            "paths": ["src/utils/placeholderImages.js"]
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to create placeholder images for the portfolio projects using our utility:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create a utility file that will provide placeholder portfolio images for our website using the placeholderImages.js utility we created earlier. This will be imported in the Portfolio component.",
            "paths": ["src/utils/portfolioData.js"]
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll modify our router setup in the main.js file to support Vue 2 compatibility:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create a router.js file to separate the routing configuration from main.js to maintain better code organization. This will define all the routes for our Vue 2 application.",
            "paths": ["src/router.js"]
        }
    }
]
```

Let me read the current content of the main.js file first:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "src/main.js"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I'll create a Footer component to complete the website layout:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Engineer2.write_new_code",
        "args": {
            "description": "Create a Footer component that will be displayed at the bottom of all pages. The footer should include links to all main pages, social media links, contact information, and copyright notice.",
            "paths": ["src/components/Footer.vue"]
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to update the App.vue file to include the Footer component we just created:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.read",
        "args": {
            "path": "src/App.vue"
        }
    }
]
```

I need to import the Footer component in App.vue:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "src/App.vue",
            "to_replace": "<script>\nexport default {",
            "new_content": "<script>\nimport Footer from './components/Footer.vue';\n\nexport default {\n  components: {\n    Footer\n  },"
        }
    }
]
```

Now I need to update the footer CSS in App.vue since we're using the Footer component instead:

```json
[
    {
        "command_name": "Editor.edit_file_by_replace",
        "args": {
            "file_name": "src/App.vue",
            "to_replace": "/* Footer Styles */
.footer {
  background-color: #1a202c;
  color: #e2e8f0;
  padding: 3rem 5% 1.5rem;
}

.footer-content {
  display: grid;
